fast-rdp-server (0.7.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * xrdp: sesman.ini sets SessionSockdirGroup=xrdp. xrdp runs as
    runtime_user/runtime_group xrdp, but sesman created /run/xrdp/<uid> with
    group root, so on every host deployed by the role X11 desktops through
    xrdp (Xfce, MATE, ...) failed with "Error connecting to X server
    [Permission denied]" in xrdp.log and a window that stayed on
    "connecting". An Ansible run fixes it, or add the line under [Security]
    in /etc/xrdp/sesman.ini and restart xrdp-sesman. Sessions started before
    keep their socket directory: fix its group (chgrp xrdp
    /run/xrdp/<uid>) or end them (backlog A7).
  * Broker, GNOME: refused at once while the user has another graphical
    session (GDM does not start a headless session then), with a message
    naming that session; a failed session unit ends the wait at once with
    its last log line instead of after 90 s, and is reset before the next
    start (also Plasma) (backlog A6).
  * Broker: running xrdp sessions the broker lost track of are found again
    through logind; an unknown xrdp session state and the reasons for
    skipping the desktop picker are logged at INFO (backlog A6).
  * Tests: proxy e2e covers the desktop picker with WaitingScreenObserve on;
    template test and host smoke check compare SessionSockdirGroup with
    runtime_group.

