fast-rdp-server (0.7.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Proxy: a client's Shutdown Request (mstsc's X in the connection bar)
    during a running session is answered with Shutdown Request Denied, as
    MS-RDPBCGR 1.3.1.4.1 requires, so mstsc disconnects cleanly instead of
    seeing a server-side drop (FreeRDP patch 0008). The next Connect in the
    same mstsc is still to be confirmed in the lab; the same symptom after a
    GNOME logout is open (backlog A5).
  * Proxy: log lines go straight to the journal through WLog's journald
    appender, in order and not torn; FreeRDP patch 0009 makes WITH_SYSTEMD
    reach winpr's config.h, the build checks for it (backlog A4).
    fastrdp-freerdp3 3.32.2-7 carries both patches.
  * Approval page: no Approve button for a login the current sign-in is too
    old for; it offers a fresh sign-in instead, at once on the login-bound
    page, without loops (backlog W6).
  * Waiting screen: the QR hint names no device.
  * Setup: fastrdp-setup offers code_or_web (realm, client, secret, CA) and
    preflight checks the Keycloak code check; fastrdp-mfa-kcadm.sh sets up
    the code check (--otp-client). make lint also checks the kcadm example
    and the PAM test script.
  * Docs: debian/changelog always carries the version of the git release.

