fast-rdp-server (0.7.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * MFA mode code_or_web (opt-in): the RDP waiting screen shows a masked field
    for the authenticator code next to the QR code of the web approval
    (passkeys); the first answer wins. Nothing is appended to the password,
    so Kerberos NLA logins work unchanged. The broker checks the code at
    Keycloak through a direct grant on its own confidential client
    (username + code, no password) and ends that session at once; limits
    per login and per user. Users without TOTP get a clean refusal from a
    Keycloak condition (no attempt counted, field closes). Safeguards: the
    setup script compares the flow exactly on every run, and the broker
    refuses tokens without otp in amr. Real RDP clients not yet tested
    (docs/lab-waiting-screen-input.md).
  * Proxy module: lab-only InputTrace switch (fastrdp_proxy_input_trace,
    default off) logs the kind of each waiting-screen input event, never
    its value.
  * Docs: passwordless policy update warning, enrolment gap (account
    console flow override), realms with password or passkey sign-in,
    approving RDP logins with the default flow (password asked again,
    Keycloak username must equal the RDP account); backlog W2-W5.

